silm:instances_papers_07_the_canonical_question_chapters_04_cheese_trap_and_identity_sections_01_five_collapse_failures_concrete_anchor_7#mittensanswerabilityprofile silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensAnswerabilityProfile is the answerability profile Hom_O(Q_07, -) reading the canonical question as the set of admitted typed-answer arrows. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol '\\Hom_{\\C}(-,A)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
